.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt DTLSV1_GET_TIMEOUT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm DTLSv1_get_timeout
.Nd determine when a DTLS or QUIC SSL object next needs a timeout event to be handled
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft int
.Fo DTLSv1_get_timeout
.Fa "SSL *s"
.Fa "struct timeval *tv"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn DTLSv1_get_timeout
can be used on a DTLS or QUIC SSL object to determine when the SSL
object next needs to perform internal processing due to the passage of
time.
.Pp
Calling
.Fn DTLSv1_get_timeout
results in
.Em *tv
being written with an amount of time left before the SSL object needs
have
.Xr DTLSv1_handle_timeout 3
called on it.
If the SSL object needs to be ticked immediately,
.Em *tv
is zeroed and the function succeeds, returning 1. If no timeout is
currently active, this function returns 0.
.Pp
This function is only applicable to DTLS and QUIC objects.
It fails if called on any other kind of SSL object.
.Pp
Note that the value output by a call to
.Fn DTLSv1_get_timeout
may change as a result of other calls to the SSL object.
.Pp
Once the timeout expires,
.Xr DTLSv1_handle_timeout 3
should be called to handle any internal processing which is due; for
more information, see
.Xr DTLSv1_handle_timeout 3 .
.Pp
.Xr SSL_get_event_timeout 3
supersedes all use cases for this this function and may be used instead
of it.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
On success, writes a duration to
.Em *tv
and returns 1.
.Pp
Returns 0 on failure, or if no timeout is currently active.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr DTLSv1_handle_timeout 3 ,
.Xr SSL_get_event_timeout 3 ,
.Xr ssl 7
